msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:12
msgid ""
"ROS documentation uses specific terminology to describe its tools, concepts, "
"software structure, and community processes. This article provides a "
"glossary of commonly used ROS terms, helping you understand key definitions "
"and follow related documentation more easily."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:25
msgid "Glossary of terms used throughout this documentation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:28
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:30
msgid ""
"An API, or Application Programming Interface, is an interface that is "
"provided by an \"application\", which in this case is usually a shared "
"library or other language appropriate shared resource. APIs are made up of "
"files that define a contract between the software using the interface and "
"the software providing the interface. These files typically manifest as "
"header files in C and C++ and as Python files in Python. In either case it "
"is important that APIs are grouped and described in documentation and that "
"they are declared as either public or private. Public interfaces are subject "
"to change rules and changes to the public interfaces prompt a new version "
"number of the software that provides them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:35
msgid "client_library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:37
msgid ""
"A client library is an :term:`API` that provides access to the ROS graph "
"using primitive middleware concepts like Topics, Services, and Actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:38
msgid "package"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:40
msgid ""
"A single unit of software, including source code, build system files, "
"documentation, tests, and other associated resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:41
msgid "REP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:43
msgid ""
"Robotics Enhancement Proposal. A document that describes an enhancement, "
"standardization, or convention for the ROS community. The associated REP "
"approval process allows the community to iterate on a proposal until some "
"consensus has been made, at which point it can be ratified and implemented, "
"which then becomes documentation. All REPs are viewable from the `REP index "
"<https://reps.openrobotics.org/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:47
msgid "VCS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:49
msgid "Version Control System, such as CVS, SVN, git, mercurial, etc..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:50
msgid "rclcpp"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:52
msgid ""
"The C++ specific :term:`Client Library <client_library>` for ROS. This "
"includes any middleware related APIs as well as the related message "
"generation of C++ data structures based on interface definitions like "
"Messages, Services, and Actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:54
msgid "repository"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:56
msgid ""
"A collection of packages usually managed using a :term:`VCS` like git or "
"mercurial and usually hosted on a site like GitHub or BitBucket. In the "
"context of this document, repositories usually contain one or more |"
"packages| of one type or another."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:58
msgid "Buffer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:60
msgid ""
"``rosidl::Buffer<T>``, the in-memory container used by generated C++ "
"messages for variable-length primitive array fields (``uint8[]``, "
"``float32[]``, ...). It behaves like a ``std::vector<T>`` by default and "
"supports pluggable memory backends so that vendors can back those fields "
"with non-CPU memory. See :doc:`../ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-"
"interfaces/Buffer-Backends/About-Buffer-Backends`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:63
msgid "Buffer backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:65
msgid ""
"A ``pluginlib`` plugin, implementing the ``rosidl::BufferBackend`` "
"interface, that teaches the RMW how to transport a ``rosidl::Buffer`` whose "
"storage lives in a vendor-specific memory domain (for example, GPU memory)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:66
msgid "Tensor message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:68
msgid ""
"A normal ROS 2 message, such as ``tensor_msgs/msg/ExperimentalTensor``, that "
"carries tensor metadata and stores the raw tensor bytes in a ``uint8[]`` "
"field backed by ``rosidl::Buffer``. Libraries such as ``torch_conversions`` "
"can map these messages to framework-native tensor types while the underlying "
"bytes use a regular buffer backend such as ``cpu`` or ``cuda``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:70
msgid "Buffer descriptor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:72
msgid ""
"A normal ROS 2 ``.msg`` produced by a ``BufferBackend`` that travels on the "
"wire in place of the raw ``uint8[]`` contents of a buffer-backed field. "
"Serialized descriptors must not exceed ``rosidl::kMaxBufferDescriptorSize`` "
"(4096 bytes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:74
msgid "Acceptable backend list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Get-Started/Glossary.rst:76
msgid ""
"The value of ``rclcpp::SubscriptionOptions::acceptable_buffer_backends`` (or "
"``acceptable_buffer_backends`` in ``rclpy``). A comma-separated list of "
"backend names the subscription is willing to receive; ``\"cpu\"`` (or empty) "
"means CPU-only, ``\"any\"`` means any installed backend, and CPU is always "
"implicitly acceptable. See :doc:`../ROS-Framework/interfaces/Working-with-"
"interfaces/Buffer-Backends/Using-Buffer-Backends`."
msgstr ""
